msgstr "![A second-order Trotter Krylov circuit with four evolution steps.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/skqd-14.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"sample-bitstrings-from-the-krylov-circuits\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "6. Sample bitstrings from the Krylov circuits {#6-sample-bitstrings-from-the-krylov-circuits}"
msgstr "6. Échantillonner des chaînes de bits à partir des circuits de Krylov {#6-sample-bitstrings-from-the-krylov-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "On hardware, you would run the transpiled circuits and measure. This is the noiseless (statevector) version of that step, showing the bitstrings SKQD would collect. Simulate each untranspiled [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") with [`ffsim.apply_unitary()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.apply_unitary.html#ffsim.apply_unitary \"(in ffsim)\") and sample the resulting statevector with [`ffsim.sample_state_vector()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.sample_state_vector.html#ffsim.sample_state_vector \"(in ffsim)\").\n"
msgstr "Sur du matériel, tu exécuterais les circuits transpilés et tu mesurerais. Voici la version sans bruit (vecteur d'état) de cette étape, qui montre les chaînes de bits que SKQD collecterait. Simule chaque [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") non transpilé avec [`ffsim.apply_unitary()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.apply_unitary.html#ffsim.apply_unitary \"(in ffsim)\") et échantillonne le vecteur d'état obtenu avec [`ffsim.sample_state_vector()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.sample_state_vector.html#ffsim.sample_state_vector \"(in ffsim)\").\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") gate is validate-then-rotate under simulation (it checks that the incoming state occupies its reference determinant, then applies the rotation). Therefore, the input is the plain occupation determinant: the lowest `nocc` modes filled per spin, with no rotation. The gate applies `reference_rotation` itself.\n"
msgstr "Une porte [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") fonctionne en simulation selon le principe valider puis tourner (elle vérifie que l'état entrant occupe son déterminant de référence, puis applique la rotation). Par conséquent, l'entrée est le simple déterminant d'occupation : les `nocc` modes les plus bas remplis par spin, sans rotation. La porte applique elle-même `reference_rotation`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pooling the samples from all five Krylov circuits, the support is tiny: a few hundred distinct bitstrings out of the $\\binom{8}{4}^2 = 4900$ determinants in the `(4, 4)` sector. This concentration, a direct consequence of the momentum-basis sparsity established in step 2, makes the subsequent classical diagonalization tractable.\n"
msgstr "En regroupant les échantillons des cinq circuits de Krylov, le support est minuscule : quelques centaines de chaînes de bits distinctes sur les $\\binom{8}{4}^2 = 4900$ déterminants du secteur `(4, 4)`. Cette concentration, conséquence directe de la parcimonie en base des impulsions établie à l'étape 2, rend tractable la diagonalisation classique qui suit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Plotting the counts with [`qiskit.visualization.plot_histogram()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.visualization.plot_histogram) makes the sparsity visible. A few configurations dominate, led by the reference determinant.\n"
msgstr "Tracer les comptages avec [`qiskit.visualization.plot_histogram()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.visualization.plot_histogram) rend la parcimonie visible. Quelques configurations dominent, en tête desquelles le déterminant de référence.\n"

